; Presentation names the living-directed output's book; it carries no body
; or sender. Transcript content ownership is deliberately not declared.
;
; Send is how a flow sends a request to a metaflow, through Flow itself.
; It carries no sender: the Nexus reads the calling process from its own
; socket and names the flow it runs in, by the Herdr pane it or its nearest
; marked ancestor runs in, or, for a Codex flow, by the thread the Codex
; app-server named in the environment of the command it started. The
; sender's metaflow must be Awake as that flow. The recipient is the Address
; the Send names and must be a metaflow Flow holds; a recipient Address whose
; topic is not an uncapitalized camelCase identifier is refused TopicRefused,
; carrying the topic as written. Priority determines delivery: an Awake recipient receives
; every priority immediately and HardAbrupt alone interrupts; an Asleep
; recipient queues Soft and is woken by MiddleAbrupt or HardAbrupt. A native
; receipt settles a Send as Delivered; submission without that receipt remains
; Attempting or Uncertain and is never retried blindly.
; DeliverAll asks Flow to deliver every queued message for an Address and does
; not insert a prompt when that queue is empty.
;
; Launch starts the metaflow at Address from its declaration in Flow's
; configuration (the meta Metaflows family): its system and user modules,
; the native model configured for its Address's Model, the effort its
; Model runs at, and its default leave-outs. The InstructionPrompt is the brief, the
; one string given that flow alone. A Launch addressed to a metaflow Awake
; as a live flow, whoever sends it, is a Replace of that flow whose
; successor is the Launch's, and it waits for the flow's idle event. A flow
; that rests now is replaced at once. A working one answers LaunchPending
; at once: the replacement is recorded with the Launch's profile, kept by a
; Nexus that starts again, and Observe.Launch follows it to its outcome.
; Until the flow rests it still receives what is sent to it; then, under
; the metaflow's lock, the successor is started with the Launch's brief and
; confirmed, the flow it replaces ends, given no turn, and the queue goes
; to the successor, oldest first; the outcome is Replaced. Any other Launch
; is a Start. An Address with no declaration is refused,
; StartRejected.Undeclared.
;
; A flow rests when its turn has ended and no work it started is in
; flight: a Claude flow at a Stop whose BackgroundWork is empty, its turn
; shown ended; a Codex flow when its app-server's thread rests.
;
; BindSeat binds the seat the calling process runs in to Address. The seat
; is read from the caller's Herdr pane: its harness and native session.
; Its FlowId is the claim for that native session, the one Flow itself
; makes when it launches a flow, so a seat Flow did not start still has
; its real id. The seat is recorded live in its pane and the metaflow Awake
; as it; a metaflow Awake as another live flow is refused Taken.
;
; Adopt binds that same authenticated seat to Address only when the native
; session supplied by the seat is the NativeSessionId in the request. The
; caller supplies no FlowId: Flow derives it from the verified native session.
;
; Refresh ends the flow the metaflow at Address is Awake as. Anybody may
; refresh a metaflow but a protected one (below), the flow itself included.
; A refresh waits for the flow's idle event: a flow that rests now is
; refreshed at once; a working one answers RefreshQueued at once, the
; refresh recorded and kept by a Nexus that starts again, and it is
; refreshed when it rests, receiving until then what is sent to it. At
; its rest Flow takes the metaflow's lock: from then nothing is
; delivered to it, and a Send that arrives queues on the metaflow. A
; metaflow whose declaration is Maintained, or whose queue holds a request
; that asks for a wake, has its successor started in the same event: the
; successor is started and its receipt confirmed before the flow it
; replaces is reaped, and the queue goes to it, oldest first. Any other is
; left Asleep, and its successor starts on the next waking request, as any
; Asleep metaflow wakes, with the whole queue, oldest first. Either way
; the ending flow's harness is closed without a turn, the flow is recorded
; ended and joins Past, and the lock is released; Refreshed names the
; Address and the flow that ended. A successor owed is recorded in Flow's
; memory before it starts, and given when it is confirmed: a Nexus that
; starts with one still owed starts it, whatever the context of the flow
; it follows. A successor whose Replace is refused answers
; SuccessorRefused with that rejection; one no declaration or configured
; model names answers Undeclared; one whose launch is still pending or
; ambiguous when the confirmation wait ends answers SuccessorUnconfirmed,
; and stays owed.
;
; A Task (flow_ethos Request) is an order with its Minutes: Flow keeps it,
; named by the LogicalDeliveryId it answers the send with, and when the
; minutes lapse with no Done naming it, sends its sender Soft.Notice with
; Wake, then again every Minutes, four reminders in all; with the last, the
; sender is sent the task's failure. Flow owns the Minutes rule at
; admission: Minutes of zero is refused MinutesRefused.Zero, below zero
; MinutesRefused.Negative, and a deadline that overflows the clock, computed
; with checked arithmetic, MinutesRefused.Unreachable; no policy maximum
; exists. Text that is no integer, or an integer beyond i64, is the CLI's
; compose Error and never reaches Flow. A Done naming the task closes it; a
; Done naming no open task is refused NoOpenTask.
;
; Restart closes a live flow's harness and resumes the same native session
; in a new pane, keeping its FlowId, session, Model and transcript, with the
; current launch configuration, modules and hooks of its Address aimed at
; this Nexus, and no prompt typed. Anybody may restart a flow, as anybody
; may refresh one; the Nexus derives the origin from the calling process,
; and a flow asking for its own restart is refused Unsupported. Only a
; Claude flow, Awake and resting, is restarted: Codex, Asleep, a working
; seat, a past flow and a restart asked by the flow itself are Unsupported.
; While its restart is under way the flow's Address is held: a Send queues,
; and the queue is handed to the resumed seat once it is bound. Restarted
; names the flow, resumed and bound. A refusal names why: UnknownFlow,
; NoHeldSession (no native session recorded), TranscriptAbsent, Busy (a
; launch, wake, hand-over or restart is under way for it), CloseRefused
; (the old harness was not shown closed), ResumeRefused (the resume or its
; bind failed, with its fixed category; session, queue and custody kept),
; Interrupted (a spawn's outcome is unproven; only Stop clears it).
;
; A protected Address (the meta ProtectedAddresses) is restarted, refreshed
; or replaced on this socket only when its own seat asks, the Nexus reading
; that seat from the calling process as it reads a restart's origin; a
; Launch of it is such a Replace. Its Stop is taken from its own seat and
; from the owner, a process in no flow's pane. Any other caller is refused
; Protected: RestartRefusal.Protected names the flow; RefreshRejection,
; ReplaceRejection and StopRejection carry Protected alone. A protected
; Address's flow is never refreshed for its threshold.
;
; Flow ordinary Signal.
;
; Start and Replace carry a LaunchProfile; a Replace's profile names the
; replaced flow as its predecessor. Neither carries its origin: the Nexus
; derives it from the calling process as Identify does (its pane's bound
; flow and that flow's native session), and a caller that is no bound flow,
; such as a deploy script, is an Unbound origin, recorded, never refused.
; A launch's harness is the one whose configured endpoint serves its model
; (Codex), else Claude; it is not named in the profile. The successor is launched; once it has
; Started, the predecessor is Stopped and taken out of receiving, and
; only then is the successor routable. Reaping belongs to the refresh
; event: no state holds both flows routable. Replaced carries the
; stopped predecessor's FlowId and the successor's Started.
; ReplaceRejection names why no replacement took place; after
; ReapRefused the successor is not routable. A Replace runs under its
; metaflow's lock, and one whose metaflow a refresh or a waking holds is
; refused Locked. A Replace asked from outside waits for its
; predecessor's idle event as a Launch does, answering LaunchPending while
; its predecessor works. Its successor is owed, as a Refresh's is, until it
; is confirmed.
;
; LaunchStatus answers a known LaunchRequestId with one LaunchInspected
; snapshot: its LaunchAttempt, its optional settled outcome, and the
; FlowNode actually recorded for the launched flow, if one exists. A
; pending attempt has no outcome. A replacement's FlowNode is its
; successor, never the predecessor named in LaunchProfile. An unknown
; request has neither attempt nor outcome; an outcome without an attempt
; is InconsistentRecords. If the rows change while read, the answer is
; ReadViewChanged. The snapshot is marker-consistent, not a transaction.
;
; Observe.Launch opens an exchange that goes on answering: on open it
; sends what LaunchStatus would, then one LaunchInspected frame for
; every later phase change, and it ends after the inspection carrying
; the outcome. Nothing is re-read on a timer; a launch that does not
; move sends nothing. Every other query is answered with exactly one
; frame.
;
; Nothing on this socket writes into a pane. Flow is the only pane writer,
; and it writes only through the privileged Deliver and Command of the
; meta contract, under its own per-pane lease.
;
; Observe.Agent opens an exchange that goes on answering: on open it
; sends the flow's agent state as Herdr shows it now, then one
; AgentObserved frame for every later change Herdr announces, and it
; ends after the frame carrying Gone, when the flow's bound pane has left
; Herdr or the flow is no longer live. Nothing is re-read on a timer. A
; flow Flow does not hold answers one Gone frame. Unknown is Herdr's own
; word for an agent it cannot read.
;
; A frame on this socket that does not decode as a Query of this contract,
; the Report of a hook built on an earlier one among them, is answered
; FrameRefused and recorded. Its UndecodableFrame names the calling process
; and its seat as Flow read them, from the kernel and from Herdr
; (SeatEvidence), and the flow bound to that seat when there is one; nothing
; in the frame is read. An earlier client cannot read the answer, so the
; record is how its refusal is seen.
;
; Observe.Undecodable opens an exchange that goes on answering: on open it
; sends every UndecodableFrame Flow recorded, oldest first, then one
; UndecodableObserved frame for each it records later, and it ends when the
; observer goes. Nothing is re-read on a timer.
;
; A Pending flow becomes Active when it is witnessed live: on a
; Presented Deliver, or when List finds its bound pane present in Herdr.
; Nothing else promotes it.
;
; A flow's lifecycle is what List reports of it. Pending and Active are
; live: a bound native seat answers. Pending is a seat not yet witnessed
; live; Active is one that has been.
;
; The three ways a flow stops being live are distinct, and each names
; who ended it. Stopped is Flow's own act: Stop, a refresh, a sleep, or a
; replacement's reap, closed a pane Flow was holding. Exited is the seat's
; own act or its accident: its harness is gone and Flow never ended it, so
; nothing can be sent to it. Retired is an owner's act: the flow is
; taken out of Flow's receiving deliberately, through the privileged
; Retire. A pane going away never makes a flow Retired — an exit retains
; the flow's record and says only that it Exited; retirement comes from
; authority, never from an observation. No pane outlives its flow: in the
; event that ends a flow, whichever of the three, Flow closes the flow's
; harness and its Herdr pane where they are still there.
;
; None of the three is a deletion: every one of them keeps the flow's
; row, its origin and its history, and none is ever reported with an
; Available route. Only Pending and Active ever are.
;
; ResolveCaller names the flow bound to the process that called: the
; Nexus reads the caller from its own socket, never from the payload.
; The optional FlowId is the caller's claim, checked against the
; binding: CallerMismatch carries the Caller the binding names.
;
; Bind binds the calling process to an Address. A Bind for { Field message
; Astra } is accepted only when the kernel-reported executable is the
; configured MessageNexusBinary; an unconfigured Nexus answers
; NotConfigured and another executable answers NotMessage. The Process in
; the request is not proof of the caller's executable.
;
; Lock, Deliver and Release are accepted only from the exact bound Message
; process (PID and start time). Message's Identify result supplies the
; distinct Sender Address in Lock; Flow trusts that bound Message peer's
; assertion and does not independently resolve the Sender's origin. A
; Sender must name an existing Awake metaflow. The request is queued with
; that Sender (QueuedRequest.{ SentBy Request }), and a woken or drained
; flow reads each queued request with who sent it; a request queued before
; senders were kept reads SentBy Unknown. Unknown addresses are not
; created; an Asleep Sender is refused as Asleep.
;
; IdentifyThread names the metaflow a Codex thread runs as, for an MCP
; send server serving that thread. Message sends it, as it sends Identify,
; with the process its own socket reports for the send server and the
; thread id Codex stamped on the tool call (its _meta threadId). Flow
; accepts it only from the bound Message process, and only when that
; process's kernel-reported executable is a configured send server's and
; its parent's is the Codex app-server executable configured with it (the
; meta SendServers family): another executable or parent is NotSendServer,
; and no configured send server is NotConfigured. The thread then names the
; Address of the metaflow Awake as the one live Codex flow whose thread Flow
; recorded at its Start; any other thread, or one whose metaflow is not
; Awake, is Unidentified. Neither the process's environment nor the
; app-server as a whole names a flow.
;
; Report carries one harness event of a flow Flow holds, sent by the
; harness's hook through the Flow CLI with the FlowId the flow was
; launched with. Flow stores the event in that flow's Memory and answers
; Reported. A FlowId Flow does not hold is refused, Refused.Unknown.FlowId,
; never adopted: a flow Flow did not launch is a flow Flow does not know.
;
; Stopped carries the BackgroundWork its hook was given: a Claude flow
; whose Stop names work in flight has not rested, and the Stop its turn
; ends with when that work has ended, Claude waking it for that, is its
; rest.
;
; Stopped and PromptSubmitted carry the native identity the harness gave
; its hook: the session, and for a Stop the transcript it writes. Flow
; acts on such an event only when that identity is the flow's registered
; native binding; any other is recorded and acts on nothing. A field the
; harness did not give is None, never an invented empty value.
; PromptSubmitted carries the SHA-256 of the submitted prompt, after the
; harness's own paste wrapper is taken off, and the harness's prompt id
; when it gave one: an exact digest of the whole prompt is the receipt
; that the harness took one queued request, and no prompt text travels.
;
; A LaunchProfile names the Address of the seat it launches. When the
; launch is confirmed, the Nexus records that Address's metaflow Awake as
; the launched flow, under the rules Bind applies: a metaflow Awake as a
; live flow is refused (AddressAwake), and an Asleep one, or one Awake as
; a flow no longer live, is taken over, a displaced flow joining Past. A replacement takes over
; the metaflow of the predecessor its profile names. A Start whose Address
; would be refused is refused before anything launches.
;
; Launched is what Start answers, carried by the Started reply; it was
; named Started until 9.0.0, when Event's Started took that name. It names
; the flow, its native session and the Herdr route it runs in (Available
; while its pane is held, Unavailable once it is gone), so the caller can
; register the seat with its messenger.
;
; A LaunchProfile names its seat's context only by module identity:
; SystemModules for the system prompt and UserModules for the first USER
; message. Flow has the context composer resolve those identities in the
; context repositories and verifies the answer; no path and no context
; text travels in a Start. The only text a Start carries is the seat's
; first brief, InstructionPrompt.
;
; The first USER message is the composed modules followed by the brief,
; sent once. When it does not fit one message it is split on module
; boundaries into PromptParts, each naming itself part k of n; the brief is
; in the last. A part after the first is sent only after the seat finished
; its answer to the one before. The durable PromptDeliveryIntent holds
; every part's SHA-256 in order, how many parts were submitted, and the
; count of Stop reports seen when the last one was. The receipt is every
; part observed in order as a user turn, then the seat's first answer at
; the intended model and effort.

